  "content": {
    "id": "p73-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "The area $S\\text{ cm}^2$ occupied by a mould satisfies\n$$\\frac{dS}{dt}=\\frac{1}{20}S(40-S),\\qquad S(0)=1,$$\nwith $t$ in days.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p73-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{S(40-S)}=\\frac{1}{40}\\left(\\frac{1}{S}+\\frac{1}{40-S}\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{40}\\left(\\frac{1}{S}+\\frac{1}{40-S}\\right)=\\frac{(40-S)+S}{40S(40-S)}=\\frac{1}{S(40-S)}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{40}\\left(\\frac{1}{S}+\\frac{1}{40-S}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{40}\\cdot\\frac{(40-S)+S}{S(40-S)}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{40}\\cdot\\frac{40}{S(40-S)}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{S(40-S)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\displaystyle S=\\frac{40}{1+39e^{-2t}}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle t=\\frac12\\ln\\left|\\frac{S}{40-S}\\right|+D$, so $\\displaystyle\\frac{S}{40-S}=Ae^{2t}$. Using $S(0)=1$ gives $A=\\frac1{39}$, hence $\\displaystyle S=\\frac{40}{1+39e^{-2t}}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dt}{dS}&=\\frac{20}{S(40-S)}\\\\&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac1S+\\frac1{40-S}\\right)\\\\t&=\\frac12\\left(\\ln|S|-\\ln|40-S|\\right)+D\\\\&=\\frac12\\ln\\left|\\frac{S}{40-S}\\right|+D\\\\\\frac{S}{40-S}&=Ae^{2t}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $S(0)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{40-1}&=Ae^0\\\\A&=\\frac1{39}.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{S}{40-S}&=\\frac{e^{2t}}{39}\\\\39S&=(40-S)e^{2t}\\\\S(39+e^{2t})&=40e^{2t}\\\\S&=\\frac{40e^{2t}}{39+e^{2t}}\\\\&=\\frac{40}{1+39e^{-2t}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "State the limiting area.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$40\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "worked": "As $t\\to\\infty$, $e^{-2t}\\to0$, so $\\displaystyle S\\to\\frac{40}{1+0}=40$. The limiting area is $40\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the time at which the area is increasing most rapidly. Give your answer to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle t=\\frac12\\ln39\\approx1.83$ days.",
          "worked": "The rate $\\displaystyle\\frac{dS}{dt}=\\frac1{20}S(40-S)$ is a quadratic in $S$ with its maximum at $S=20$, half the carrying capacity.\n$$\\begin{align*}20&=\\frac{40}{1+39e^{-2t}}\\\\1+39e^{-2t}&=2\\\\e^{2t}&=39\\\\t&=\\frac12\\ln39\\\\&\\approx1.83\\text{ days}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
  },
